              {
                "id": 2779969,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Ratan Lal, a soil scientist from Ohio State University in The USA, claims that the world's agricultural soils could potentially absorb 13% of the carbon dioxide in the atmosphere, the equivalent of the amount released in the last thirty years, and research is going on into how this might be achieved.",
