"gf_35\">______</span></p>\n<p>●&nbsp; &nbsp;e.g. through year-round planting and increasing the <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_36\">______</span> of plants that are grown</p>\n<p><strong>California study:</strong></p>\n<p>●&nbsp; &nbsp;taking place on a big <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_37\">______</span> farm</p>\n<p>●&nbsp; &nbsp;uses compost made from waste from agriculture and <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_38\">______</span></p>\n<p><strong>Australia study:</strong></p>\n<p>●&nbsp; &nbsp;aims to increase soil carbon by using <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_39\">______</span> that are always green</p>\n<p><strong>Future developments may include:</strong></p>\n<p>●&nbsp; &nbsp;reducing the amount of fertilizer used in farming</p>\n<p>●&nbsp; &nbsp;giving farmers <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_40\">______</span> for carbon storage, as well as their produce</p>",
